A||||4||Fiero SE||Does anyone know what might be the problem?||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero SE||12-05-1999||07:57 PM||||Ok, we have an 84 fiero se auto and when you accelerate it makes this clicking sound, you can accelerate slow and it won't (usually) make it but it isn't continuous. We took it to the shop and they said it might be the trans axle. Has anyone else had this problem and know how or how much it will cost to fix it? please let me know. you can e-mail me at  <A HREF="mailto:Alex985@aol.com">Alex985@aol.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||12-05-1999||08:55 PM||||A clicking noise from the tranny area could be a bad axle CV joint. That's better than a bad tranny.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Trixi||12-05-1999||11:15 PM||||hello<BR>It sounds like a bad cv joint, but it could also be a trannie problem<BR>If it slips or anything like that it is a trannie prob||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan||12-06-1999||04:43 AM|||| Usually a bad cv joint will make a worse cliking in the turns and heavy acceleration.Check the cv boot and see if it is cracked and hence thrown out the grease.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MCordray||12-06-1999||07:07 PM||||I had the same problem with my '88 coupe. It ended up being a worn out dog-bone. The lack of engine support caused the exhaust pipe to clack against the frame upon acceleration, specifically when turning. You may have the same problem. Couldn't hurt to check it out.||||reg||1
